### List the members of the organization (Owner only). First log in with http/auth.http and paste the token.
# Expect 200 {"items":[{"id","name","email","role","isActive","lastLoginAt","allWarehouses","warehouses":[{"id","code"}]}],"total","page","pageSize"}.
# The Owner comes first (allWarehouses true), then the others by name. No passwordHash and no reset columns.
GET http://localhost:3000/api/members?page=1&pageSize=20
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Warehouse Admin or Viewer: 403 FORBIDDEN
GET http://localhost:3000/api/members
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Change a member's role and warehouses (Owner only). Use an "id" from GET /api/members.
# Expect 200 with the updated member (same shape as a list row). The change applies on the member's next request.
PATCH http://localhost:3000/api/members/00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000000
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "role": "VIEWER", "warehouseIds": [] }

### Deactivate a member (only false is accepted; the member's existing token gets 401 at once)
PATCH http://localhost:3000/api/members/00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000000
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "isActive": false }

### The Owner cannot be changed
# Expect 409 CONFLICT when the ID is the Owner's. The role OWNER in the body is 400.
PATCH http://localhost:3000/api/members/00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000000
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "role": "OWNER" }
